2. द्रा cl. 2. P. द्रा॑ति (Impv. द्रा॑तु, द्रा॑न्तु, RV.; AV.; pf. दद्रुर्, p. Ā. दद्राण॑, RV. ; aor. अद्रासीत्; Subj. द्रासत्, ib.),
to run, make haste:
Caus. द्रापयति (Desid. of Caus. दि॑द्रापयिषति), ŚBr.;
 aor. अदिद्रपत्, Siddh. :
Intens. द॑रिद्राति, TS.; 3. pl. दरिद्रति, Hit.;
to run hither and thither;
to be in need or poor:
 Desid. of Intens. दिदरिद्रासति and दिदरिद्रिषति, Pāṇ. vi, 1, 14,

Nom. P. ˚यति, to make firm, fasten, tighten, strengthen, Uttarar. ii, 27;
 confirm, assert, L., Sch.;
to stop, restrain, Śārṅg. (cf. डृढय).

cl. 1. P. द्र॑मति (Naigh. ii, 14) to run about, roam, wander, Dhātup. xiii, 23;
 pf. दद्रमुर्, Bhaṭṭ. :
Intens. दन्द्रम्यते id., KaṭhUp. ii, 5. [cf. √ द्रा and 2. द्रु; Gk. ἔ-δραμ-ον, δέ-δρομ-α, δρόμος.]

cl. 1. P. द्राखति, to become dry or arid;
to be able or competent;
to adorn;
to prohibit or prevent, Dhātup. v, 10 (cf. ध्राक्).

cl. 1. Ā. द्राघते, to be able;
to stretch, lengthen;
to exert one's self;
to be tired;
to tire, torment;
to roam, stroll, Dhātup. iv, 40 :
Caus. द्राघयति, to lengthen (also prosod., RPrāt.), extend, stretch, Rājat.; Bhaṭṭ.;
to be long or slow, tarry, delay, R.
